[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

Realistic BB guns, 25 real guns and ammo reloading for [b]Build 42[/b]. Part of the Dazed suite.

Version 0.5.0 has not been tested in game yet. Please report problems in the Discussions tab.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes. The server and every player need it[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedArmory[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/h-bb.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/bb.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Crossman 92 BB Pistol:[/b] CO2 powered, 18-round magazine.
[*][b]Dazey Pump Master BB Shotgun:[/b] spring pump action. Each shell throws 6 BBs and comes back empty to refill.
[*][b]Tokio Maroo M16 AEG:[/b] battery powered, semi and full auto, 60-round magazine.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/h-guns.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/guns.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Handguns:[/b] Glok 17, Rugar Mark II (.22), Kolt Pyton .357, Smith & Wessen Model 10 (.38), Remingten Double Derringer.
[*][b]Submachine guns:[/b] Heckler & Kosh MP5A3, Uzzi, M.A.K.-10, all semi and full auto.
[*][b]Rifles:[/b] Kolt AR-15A2 Sporter, Rugger 10/22, Norinko SKS, Norinko MAK-9O Sporter, M-1 Garrand, M-1 Karbine, Mozin-Nagant 91/3O, Marlen 336C, Winchelster Model 7O.
[*][b]Shotguns:[/b] Remingten 1100 (semi-auto), Franki SPAZ-12, Ithaka 37 Featherlight.
[*][b]Heavy:[/b] Brawning M-2HB "Ma Deuce" .50 for the tripod, FM Meanie M-249 SAW, Barrette M-82A1 .50 rifle.
[*][b]Odd ones:[/b] the Oryon flare pistol (its flare draws zombies to where it lands) and the Paslow nailer (quiet, fires nails).
[*]Each one is built on the closest vanilla gun, so it handles, sounds and reloads like it. Real magazines, an en-bloc clip for the Garrand, a 200-round box for the SAW.
[*]Reload the Model 10, SKS or Mozin-Nagant with a loaded speedloader or stripper clip on you and it all goes in at once.
[*]Found in gun stores, pawn shops, hunting spots and homes, police and SWAT storage; the heavies only in army storage, the .50s very rarely.
[/list]

[h2]How the BB guns play[/h2]
[list]
[*]They sting more than they kill. Hits make zombies stumble; a headshot up close can drop one.
[*]Quiet: zombies hear them only a few tiles away.
[*]Good for birds, rabbits and other small game.
[*]Open a tube of BBs, load magazines or fill shells. Right-click a gun to change its CO2 cartridge or battery.
[*]Guns wear and jam more as they wear. Fix them with a BB Gun Repair Kit.
[*]Find them in toy shops, sports and gun stores, pawn shops and kids' bedrooms.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/h-reload.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/reload.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Spent brass and 12 gauge hulls come back from real guns: more of them as your Reloading skill grows.
[*]Load 9mm, .45, .38, .357, .44 and 12 gauge on an RCBX Rock Chukker or MECC 600 Jr press, or anywhere with a Lea Loader hand kit.
[*][b]New in 0.4.0:[/b] rifles too. Vanilla 5.56, 7.62x51 (.308) and .30-30, plus new .22 LR, 7.62x39, .30-06, .30 Carbine, 7.62x54R and .50 BMG rounds with their own boxes, ready for the guns to come. Small and large rifle primers, IMX 4064 rifle powder, rifle bullets and die sets.
[*].22 LR is rimfire: re-prime it with priming compound on the hand kit, and expect more duds. .50 BMG is press only and takes a lot of powder.
[*]Primers and Hodgeson Clays-Dot powder are rare finds: the real limit on home loads.
[*]Some loads come out as duds. Pull them apart with an inertia puller.
[*]Learn it at Reloading 2 (magnums and most rifles at 3, big rifles at 4, .50 BMG at 7) or from the Handloader's Digest magazine.
[*]Presses, dies, powder and primers turn up in gun, sports and hunting places, garages and police storage.
[/list]

[h2]More ammo[/h2]
[list]
[*]Link .50 BMG rounds into belts for a .50 ammo can.
[*]Make 12 gauge signal flares from spent hulls, shotshell primers and a road flare.
[*]Make nail strips from nails and glue or tape.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/h-mg.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Armory/images/mg.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]M-6O Hog:[/b] a belt-fed .308 machine gun, too heavy to fire from your hands.
[*][b]Field Tripod (M122):[/b] drop it where you want your nest (a second-floor window works), right-click it and man the gun. It turns all the way round; walk off to step away.
[*]Belts: link vanilla .308 rounds with belt links and load them into an ammo can like a magazine. Most links come back as you fire.
[*]Found in army and police storage. Very loud: expect company.
[/list]

[h2]Sandbox[/h2]
Damage, noise radius, loot rate, shots per CO2 cartridge and battery, and an optional "you'll shoot your eye out" ricochet (off by default). For reloading: brass recovery, dud rate, separate loot rates for gear, powder and primers, and "all reloading recipes known". For machine guns: fire without a mount (off by default), belt link recovery and loot rate. A loot rate for the new calibres, flares and nail strips, and one for the real guns.

